{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/698370-retconning-fun-beasts-in-other-lines-older-books","id":698370,"title":"Retconning Fun: Beasts in Other Lines/Older Books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-11T21:14:24-07:00","id":698370,"title":"Retconning Fun: Beasts in Other Lines/Older Books?","content":"When a new line, or book, or series comes out, it sometimes casts events in older works in a different light - regardless of whether either author meant for that to happen. Now that <b>Beast</b> is out, what characters in the other nWoD do you think might have met (or been!) Beasts? What events might the Begotten have been involved with?<br /> <br /> For example, I suspect that Lucian the Bodiless was a Beast with an invisibility nightmare. The mages of the Fallen Pillar (an ascetic Legacy detailed in <i>Legacies: the Sublime</i>) pass along the legend of how their founder met Lucian, and was inspired to create an entire Legacy:<br /> <br /> <i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once, there was an ascetic mage who lived atop a great column in the middle of the desert. Known only as the Pillar Saint, his magic allowed him to give up food, water, even sleep. And so he sat there, every day and night, contemplating the universe, never coming down.<br /> <br /> Until the day the creature found him. As enlightened as he was, even the Pillar Saint could not see it, only noting its presence from the sand it kicked up, and the way it disrupted the light. It introduced itself as Lucian, and asked the Pillar Saint what he was doing.<br /> <br /> As the Pillar Saint explained how he had transcended the world, and needed nothing from it, Lucian started laughing. Angered, the Pillar Saint demanded to know what was so funny. After all, he was the Pillar Saint! The mage who had risen above all earthly needs!<br /> <br /> With one great blow, Lucian shattered the column.<br /> <br /> Bones broken, paralyzed from the fall, the Pillar Saint could only listen as Lucian continued to laugh. &quot;You still needed that pillar,&quot; Lucian chortled, before leaving with the wind.<br /> <br /> As he lay there, among the ruins of the column, the Pillar Saint began to laugh himself. In falling, he had found the enlightenment he'd long sought. Despite his broken back, he stood up, and walked away. Now calling himself the Anchorite, he went forth to teach others how to shatter their own pillars and find enlightenment. </div> </div> </div></i><br /> <br /> Tell me that doesn't sound exactly like a Beast (possibly with an air- or sand- vibe), with a Hunger for Ruin or Punishment . . . or who just felt the need to take down an arrogant mage?<br /> <br /> Anyone else have any likely candidates? What other legends, myths, and stories from the World of Darkness seem to feature Beasts or their handiwork?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-12-2015, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T21:45:00-07:00","id":698394,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is still in the Beast book, but originally it had this section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Darius took his name and his hunting style from a werewolf he met once. He chases down his prey and breaks a bone \u2014 arm, leg, neck, doesn\u2019t matter, as long as he can hear the crackle. He inflicts pain and fear in his prey, and leaves behind a crippled, terrified person\u2026or sometimes just a corpse, depending on how loudly his Soul howls. </div> </div> </div>This isn't a retcon, necessarily, but the werewolf mentioned is likely Dar-us, the Slow Killer, from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane. In the fiction provided, some of the witnesses believe him to be dead, but people still seem to see him. The new Dar-us might be this Darius the Beast. If you wanted to get a cycle going on, Dar-us had his First Change when he was thirteen. He was in a hospital, 'hundreds of pins inserted into his body, unable to speak for all the metal piercing his mangled jaw.' And something came into his room, sat on his chest, and pushed, 'listening to the creaks and crunches of the bones beneath.'<br /> <br /> I think the story is particularly interesting if you view it as starting with a Beast that, enjoying its hobby and feast, then spurred Dar-us into his First Change through terror and pain, only to have Dar-us later teach another Beast his hunting style and inspire said Beast to their own path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T07:32:57-07:00","id":698616,"title":"","content":"In the <i>Horror Recognition Guide</i>, the monster from the &quot;Thing From the Deep&quot; chapter could fit the bill for a Beast Rampant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T12:09:48-07:00","id":698861,"title":"","content":"I have the Crone myth coming from vampires hearing Beast legends of the Dark Mother and, well, believing them.<br /> <br /> That extradimensional woodland from Mysterious Places sounds like a good for a Chamber in the Primordial Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T23:44:08-07:00","id":737120,"title":"","content":"I immediately thought of the Crone when I read about the dark mother but YOU SIR just made what I thought was the weakest chapter in Mysterious Places AWESOME!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}